---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Facts from "../components/Facts.astro";

const keywords = ["Tangible", "Embodied", "Distributed", "Networked", "Sound", "Interaction"];
---
<Base>
  <h1 class="thesis">The Sound of Smart Things<span>Making the Invisible Audible</span></h1>

  <h2 class="label">Abstract</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Networked smart things are part of everyday environments, yet their states, activity and relations are mostly imperceptible. TSOST investigates sound as a central interaction material in such distributed systems. Sound can be perceived without visual attention: it can stay in the periphery or move into focus, be continuous or discrete, and be directional. Following a Research through Design approach, the project designs and builds autonomous, sensing, networked, sound-producing devices, and studies what this design work reveals about the interface between the digital and the physical. The central artefact is TESI (Tangible and Embodied Sound Interaction), a modular toolkit: a sensor node, network middleware and software for real-time sensor-to-sound mapping.</p>
  </div>

  <ul class="keywords" aria-label="Keywords">
    <li class="label">Keywords</li>
    {keywords.map((k) => <li class="label">{k}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2 class="label">Project</h2>
  <Facts rows={[
    ["PhD Candidate", "Francesco Di Maggio"],
    ["Department", "Industrial Design, Eindhoven University of Technology"],
    ["Supervisors", "Bart Hengeveld, Berry Eggen"],
    ["Co-supervisor", "Rebecca Fiebrink, University of the Arts London"],
  ]} />

</Base>
